# Lagoon Breach targets only "an attacking creature you don't control" (CR 115.1, 506.4). On Bot1's turn 3 Bot1 attacks with its
# own Ornithopter while Bot2's Llanowar Elves stay home: no creature qualifies (the attacker is Bot1's own, the other is not
# attacking), so the Adventure is not offered although Bot1 has the mana. On turn 4 the Elves attack and the same cast is
# offered (the positive control, in the neighbouring Lagoon Breach scenarios) - here it is taken to prove the first refusal
# was for the target and not for the mana.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Horned Loch-Whale
Ornithopter
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
! Bot1.Hand.Horned Loch-Whale.Cast(Ability: Adventure)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Horned Loch-Whale.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves; Ability: Adventure)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Accept

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
Bot2.Library = Llanowar Elves; Forest; Forest; Forest
Exile = Horned Loch-Whale
